yptocurrency products. The company was founded in 2008 and is headquartered in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Aaron  Simons | CEO & Director | Age 44 | Compensation: $10.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $3.5M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers, improving at 16%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $483K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $98K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Virtu Financial, Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $4.8B market cap on $3.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +15% over the past three years and +16% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 29% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 22-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $496M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 14 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.11\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 9.2\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 1.8%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 5.2% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.6% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $12.0M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 59% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","10 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Financial Services peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Is Virtu Financial (VIRT) Stock Undervalued Right Now?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3025464/is-virtu-financial-virt-stock-undervalued-right-now?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_2-3025464","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793972403.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Virtu Financial Inc 